  "yt_description": "You are paying full price to resend the same prompt on every call. Prompt caching fixes that.\n\n• The provider caches the start of your prompt: tools, then system, then messages\n• Claude API: a cache read costs 0.1x the base input price (less on newer models)\n• Writing the cache costs 1.25x for the 5-minute cache\n• The cache lasts 5 minutes and every hit refreshes it at no extra cost\n• Put stable content first and the changing question last\n\n#promptcaching #aiengineering #llm #claude #softwareengineering",
  "ig_caption": "You're paying full price for the same prompt. Every. Single. Call. 💸\n\n⚡ Prompt caching stores the start of your prompt\n💰 Cache read on the Claude API = 0.1x input price\n✍️ First write = 1.25x\n⏱️ Lives 5 minutes, refreshed on every hit\n📐 Rule: stable stuff first, question last\n\nSave this before your next API bill. Follow @stackshade for more.\n\nVoiceover is AI-generated. Source: Claude API docs, prompt caching.",
